{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and To Be Loved appeal to me because expressive voices and warm melodies connect with what I enjoyed in Stages and A Musical Affair.",
    "In The Lonely Hour interests me because emotional singing fits my listening preferences, although I would sample it before choosing the album."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect with earlier listening, but I want music for everyday relaxation now rather than seasonal songs.",
    "A party-oriented album feels less suited to my current mood, while titles such as The Very Best Of and Hope give me too little information to judge their musical fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My earlier Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing interest regardless of what I want today.",
    "My interest in some country albums seems to have been extended to music with a different mood; enjoying country does not mean I am looking for party songs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choice of relaxing classical music suggests that calm, soothing listening matters to me right now.",
    "Expressive singing, melodic warmth, and vocal harmonies matter more to me than a broad connection to an album I previously chose; unfamiliar collections need enough musical context for me to judge that connection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in melodic vocal music but give too much weight to past seasonal listening and too little to my current relaxing mood."
}"}
